---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'Solar Panel Maintenance \u0026 Cleaning Guide for Thailand';
const description = 'Keep your solar panels performing at peak with our Thailand maintenance guide. Cleaning schedules, costs (300 THB/panel), monitoring apps, and annual inspection checklists.';
---
<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-solar-green">Home</a> / <span>Guides</span> / <span>Maintenance & Cleaning</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Solar Panel Maintenance & Cleaning Guide for Thailand</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-600 mb-8">
      Thailand's tropical climate means dust, pollen, bird droppings, and monsoon residue can reduce panel efficiency by 15–25%. 
      Regular cleaning and inspections keep your system producing at peak capacity.
    </p>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">How Often Should You Clean Solar Panels in Thailand?</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-orange-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-orange-200">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Dry Season (Nov–Apr)</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-700">Dust builds up fast. Clean <strong>every 2–4 weeks</strong> in dusty or agricultural areas. Urban areas: monthly.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Rainy Season (May–Oct)>/h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-700">Rain helps but leaves mineral deposits. Clean <strong>every 1–2 months</strong> to remove water spots and debris.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">DIY vs Professional Cleaning</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50">
              <th class="p-3 text-left border">Factor</th>
              <th class="p-3 text-center border">DIY Cleaning</th>
              <th class="p-3 text-center border">Professional Service</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td class="p-3 border">Cost</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">Free (water + soft brush)</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">300 THB per panel + travel</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="p-3 border">Safety</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">Risk of falls / electric shock</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">Insured, trained technicians</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-3 border">Equipment</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">Garden hose + soft cloth</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">Deionized water, soft brushes, safety gear</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="p-3 border">Inspection</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">Visual only</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">Includes crack, hotspot, wiring checks</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-3 border">Best for</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">Ground mount, easy access</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">Rooftop, large systems, warranty protection</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-2">
        <strong>Tip:</strong> Many manufacturers require professional cleaning for warranty validity. Check your panel warranty terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Safe DIY Cleaning Steps</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-2">If you clean panels yourself, follow this procedure:</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700">
        <li><strong>Shut down the system</strong> — turn off the inverter and DC isolator.</li>
        <li><strong>Rinse with plain water</strong> — use a garden hose. Avoid high-pressure sprays.</li>
        <li><strong>Gently wipe</strong> — soft microfiber cloth or sponge. No abrasives.</li>
        <li><strong>No detergents needed</strong> — they can leave residue.</li>
        <li><strong>Clean early morning or late afternoon</strong> — avoid hot panels cracking from cold water shock.</li>
        <li><strong>Never walk on panels</strong> — risk of cracks and electrical hazards.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Annual Inspection Checklist</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">Book a professional inspection once a year. Here's what should be checked:</p>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded-lg"><div class="font-bold">Visual Panel Check</div><div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Cracks, chips, discoloration, hot spots</div></div>
        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded-lg"><div class="font-bold">Wiring & Connections</div><div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Loose connections, corrosion, insulation wear</div></div>
        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded-lg"><div class="font-bold">Mounting & Racking</div><div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Bolt tightness, rust, structural integrity</div></div>
        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded-lg"><div class="font-bold">Inverter Health</div><div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Error logs, cooling fans, ventilation</div></div>
        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded-lg"><div class="font-bold">Performance Test</div><div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Compare actual vs expected output</div></div>
        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded-lg"><div class="font-bold">Monitoring System</div><div class="text-sm text-gray-600">App connectivity, sensor accuracy</div></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Thailand-Specific Issues to Watch</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-3">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-solar-green">✓</span> <span><strong>Salt corrosion (coastal areas):</strong> Near the sea? Rinse panels more frequently. Coastal areas like Trat, Phuket, and Chonburi experience accelerated frame corrosion.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-solar-green">✓</span> <span><strong>Potential Induced Degradation (PID):</strong> High heat and humidity accelerate PID in lower-quality panels. Tier 1 panels resist this better.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-solar-green">✓</span> <span><strong>Hot spots:</strong> Partial shading from trees or antennas causes localized overheating, permanently damaging cells.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-solar-green">✓</span> <span><strong>Bird droppings:</strong> Acidic and opaque. Remove within days to prevent etching and output loss.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-50 to-blue-50 rounded-xl p-8 mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Related Guides</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="/guides/solar-sunlight-hours" class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow border border-gray-100">
          <div class="font-bold">Sunlight Hours in Thailand</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Peak sun data for maintenance planning</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/guides/solar-panels-cloudy-days" class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow border border-gray-100">
          <div class="font-bold">Cloudy Day Performance</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Post-monsoon cleaning priorities</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/guides/solar-system-sizing" class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow border border-gray-100">
          <div class="font-bold">System Sizing Calculator</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Size your system for year-round production</div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="bg-solar-green text-white rounded-xl p-8 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-2">Book Your First Professional Clean</h2>
      <p class="mb-6">Our maintenance team covers all of Thailand. 300 THB per panel, travel included. Free inspection with every clean.</p>
      <a href="/#contact" class="inline-block bg-white text-solar-green font-semibold px-8 py-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-100 transition-colors">
        Book a Maintenance Clean — Contact Us
      </a>
      <p class="text-sm mt-4 opacity-80">
        Ask about our annual <a href="/" class="underline">solar panel cleaning service</a> packages.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
